<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <AssemblyName>CodeBrix.VideoPlayback.ConsumerShape</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>CodeBrix.VideoPlayback.ConsumerShape</RootNamespace>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <Nullable>disable</Nullable>
    <InvariantGlobalization>true</InvariantGlobalization>
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    THE POINT OF THIS SAMPLE is what it does NOT reference. An application that plays Vorbis-audio .cbv files
    needs the playback library and a presenter, and nothing else: no Opus package, no codec binary, no
    windowing toolkit. `dotnet publish` this project and look for CodeBrix.Audio.Opus.dll - it is not there,
    and that is the check the Phase B gate makes.

    A real application would reference the two PACKAGES; they are project references here because this sample
    lives in the repository that builds them.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\CodeBrix.VideoPlayback\CodeBrix.VideoPlayback.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\CodeBrix.VideoPlayback.Skia\CodeBrix.VideoPlayback.Skia.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Skia's managed assembly arrives with the presenter package; its NATIVE binary does not, because the
    library must not choose one for every platform an application might ship on. Choosing one is the
    APPLICATION's job, and this is an application, so it chooses the Linux build it runs on.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="SkiaSharp.NativeAssets.Linux" Version="4.151.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Nothing is linked in for the decoder. The uncompressed-video codec ships in the playback library and
    registers itself, so this sample plays its clip with no codec package installed at all. A real
    application playing a coded clip would reference a real decoder package instead.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Content Include="..\..\tests\assets\raw-vorbis.cbv">
      <Link>assets\raw-vorbis.cbv</Link>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
    </Content>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
